1
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,199
(Episode 2)

2
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,920
(This is a work of fiction.)

3
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:19,880
Who are you?

4
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:23,800
What is this place?

5
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:28,360
Don't do anything rash. I'm a barrister.

6
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,440
I can...

7
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,840
Yau Yam Yam,

8
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:35,960
I hereby declare that your life is over.

9
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,600
You were supposed to live until 70,

10
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,600
but you've committed too many sins.

11
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:41,920
Your life is cut short to 31.

12
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,480
You deserve this retribution.

13
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,120
Your crimes are...

14
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:50,360
How should I put it?

15
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,040
- Too many to list. - Far too many to list.

16
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,680
I can't be bothered to count them all.

17
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:57,840
Anyway, I sentence you to 721 counts of torture.

18
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,080
First, we'll sever your tongue.

19
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:02,640
You...

20
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:10,760
Wait.

21
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:16,480
What should I do first?

22
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:37,120
If I sever her tongue first,

23
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,000
and she can't scream, won't that be less satisfying?

24
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:43,800
Chop it off first.

25
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:47,920
Wait.

26
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,840
There's no need for theatrics in the netherworld.

27
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:52,200
Right. It's a force of habit.

28
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:57,520
King of Hell, I have a humble request.

29
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:58,920
You're interfering with my execution.

30
00:04:58,921 --> 00:05:00,520
If your reason isn't good enough,

31
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,040
I'll sever your tongue too.

32
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:07,000
Well, I want to help Yau Yam Yam return to life.

33
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:15,640
Actually, her natural lifespan hasn't ended yet.

34
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:18,680
It has just been cut short by you, Your Majesty.

35
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:22,520
If you could be a little lenient,

36
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:27,960
I believe she can return to the mortal world.

37
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:43,640
Your Majesty, please take a look.

38
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:46,640
There's more.

39
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:54,600
Fusen red soil agarwood, Indian rosewood,

40
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:59,000
Hollong tree incense, and Bome musk.

41
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,440
The four most famous fragrances in the world.

42
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:05,000
I wonder if these will make you...

43
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:07,120
a little more lenient?

44
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:12,960
Why are you helping her?

45
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,479
I want her to help me...

46
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:21,000
with my family matters in the mortal world.

47
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:25,680
Five days.

48
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,080
That's all?

49
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:36,360
Fine. Five days it is.

50
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:41,280
Thank you, Your Majesty.

51
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:43,400
Thank you, Your Majesty.

52
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:48,360
Let's go. We're leaving.

53
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:50,120
This way.

54
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:52,040
Let's go. Be careful.

55
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,040
Is this really hell?

56
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,320
The real deal.

57
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,360
Not what you expected, right?

58
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:20,960
Why did you help me?

59
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:24,720
My time is up. I can't return to life.

60
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,400
I can't handle things myself.

61
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:28,999
So I need someone...

62
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,920
who can bridge the gap between the living and the dead...

63
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,760
and is well-versed in the law to help me.

64
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:35,520
I've seen your methods.

65
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,840
You're the perfect barrister for me.

66
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:40,080
Help me distribute my estate.

67
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:45,160
I heard the King of Hell rarely lets anyone return to life.

68
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:47,080
I was just taking a chance.

69
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,640
I didn't expect it to go so smoothly.

70
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:54,880
It seems you really are special.

71
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,920
You didn't kill me just because you wanted me to help you,

72
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,560
did you?

73
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,760
With money comes insider information.

74
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:11,440
It's the same in the netherworld...

75
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,560
as it is in the world of the living.

76
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:15,920
I knew you were about to die anyway.

77
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,600
Why would I need to kill you?

78
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,920
Then do you know who killed me?

79
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:23,480
That, I don't know.

80
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:28,640
The King of Hell is fickle.

81
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:30,080
He might go back on his word.

82
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,560
I don't want to go back and have my tongue cut off.

83
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:32,880
Let's hurry up and lose them. Run.

84
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,320
Over there!

85
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:06,640
I have this.

86
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:08,600
Don't let them get away! After them!

87
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:18,440
- Lie down on it. - What?

88
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:21,760
This is where the underworld connects to the world of the living.

89
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:24,560
If you want to go back up, lie down.

90
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,240
Look up.

91
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:38,040
Has my wife...

92
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,400
come by?

93
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:48,040
I... I want to see my son.

94
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:55,280
- Where's the doctor? - He's on his way.

95
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:58,720
We can't wait. Let's start.

96
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:00,000
Mr. Shek, I'm Mr. Wong, a lawyer.

97
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,400
According to your instructions,

98
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,600
I will now formally help you...

99
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:04,680
draft your will as you wished.

100
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,160
I'll read the contents to you,

101
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:07,640
and you will sign it yourself,

102
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:10,360
witnessed by two other lawyers.

103
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:11,440
Do you understand?

104
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,160
I understand.

105
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:19,639
"I, Shek Chung,"

106
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:21,040
"hereby make my will as follows."

107
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:23,640
"I revoke all previous wills..."

108
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,079
"and declare this..."

109
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:27,320
"to be my last will and testament."

110
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,800
"I appoint my son, Shek Kwong Sing,"

111
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,080
“as the executor of my estate.”

112
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:33,440
“After deducting funeral expenses..."

113
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:35,280
"and other necessary costs,"

114
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:39,000
"I bequeath all assets to Shek Kwong Sing."

115
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:42,560
"If my wife, Kwok Miu Wah, claims any inheritance,"

116
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:44,360
"she shall be given a nominal one dollar."

117
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,640
Mr. Shek, do you understand and agree...

118
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,720
to the contents of this will?

119
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:05,800
Dad.

120
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:07,800
Dad!

121
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:12,320
Dad!

122
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:24,760
What are you doing here?

123
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,680
- Step aside. - Dad doesn't want to see you.

124
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,760
Go away!

125
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,360
Get out!

126
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:31,520
All of you, step aside!

127
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,960
Shek Chung, how dare you just die like this?

128
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,800
Dad said he doesn't want to see you! Get out!

129
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:39,280
- Shut up! Wake up! - Calm down.

130
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,799
- You can't die! - Don't touch Dad!

131
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:41,960
He has already passed away!

132
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:43,520
He's not dead yet!

133
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,840
- Wake up! - He's gone!

134
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:47,599
- Don't die! - Don't touch my dad!

135
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,600
Wake up!

136
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:51,360
He's my husband!

137
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,320
We shouldn't air dirty laundry in public.

138
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:14,120
Taking family matters to court is one thing,

139
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:16,720
but what I'm most worried about now...

140
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:19,000
is that wicked woman stealing all my money.

141
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:22,880
Counselor Yau,

142
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:26,320
I've hired you to ensure...

143
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,280
that wicked woman doesn't get a single extra dollar...

144
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,480
from my estate.

145
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:33,880
The biggest dispute in your case is that...

146
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,440
when you signed that will,

147
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:38,080
there was no doctor present...

148
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:39,320
to certify your mental state.

149
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:44,160
Based on precedents, it's a bit difficult to handle.

150
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:46,880
Don't worry, I have evidence.

151
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:49,840
When I found out that wicked woman...

152
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:51,400
was plotting to take my money,

153
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:54,560
I personally wrote a new will.

154
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:57,560
I left everything to my son.

155
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:01,800
But I softened my heart after writing it.

156
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,280
I left it in a wooden box at the office.

157
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,960
I never sent it to the law firm.

158
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:10,920
Counselor Yau, if you find this will,

159
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,600
you can prove that...

160
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:15,800
I had long intended to rewrite it.

161
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,080
I wasn't mentally unfit,

162
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:20,360
nor was I misled by my son.

163
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,880
If you really had such a will,

164
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:25,760
you should have told your son to bring it to court.

165
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:29,120
I was in a daze before I died.

166
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,600
How could I remember so much?

167
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:33,560
I only remembered after I died.

168
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:37,760
I even tried to tell my son in a dream to go look for it.

169
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:40,200
But that son of mine is so useless.

170
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:58,120
You brat, stop building those models.

171
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,800
I left a will at the office.

172
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:00,880
Go find it!

173
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:06,600
Why are you sleeping here?

174
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:09,320
I dreamt I was building a Freedom model.

175
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,440
The one you said was hard to build?

176
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:14,840
I want to finish it. Let me sleep more.

177
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:16,920
Can't you just appear...

178
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,840
before your son directly like this?

179
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,040
Do you think seeing a ghost is that easy?

180
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,160
Certain conditions must be met.

181
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:27,200
Either you've just died,

182
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,040
or you're like yourself,

183
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:31,640
with a very strong yin energy.

184
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:36,840
So you want me...

185
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:40,000
to help you find the draft of the will...

186
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,080
for your son?

187
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:44,440
Exactly. You've got it.

188
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:47,840
You can see ghosts, and you're a lawyer.

189
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:50,040
The unscrupulous kind, at that.

190
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:52,280
You'll surely find a way...

191
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:54,560
to stop that woman from getting my money.

192
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Is there a problem?

193
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:04,640
Not with you.

194
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:06,040
But what about the King of Hell?

195
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:08,200
Doesn't he want to take me back?

196
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:11,280
Are you sure he'll let me stay here?

197
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,720
Don't worry, I've already appeased him.

198
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:16,920
How did you appease him?

199
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:25,320
Your Majesty, is something wrong?

200
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:26,879
I've been thinking.

201
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:28,640
Returning to the mortal world is a serious matter.

202
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:30,400
This deal doesn't seem quite right.

203
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:34,280
Yes, I understand.

204
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:38,280
I wonder if this would be more appropriate.

205
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:42,960
Let me remind you.

206
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:44,640
Keep a close eye on Yau Yam Yam.

207
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:47,280
If she does anything bad again,

208
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,240
I'll bring her back at any time.

209
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:51,800
Yes.

210
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:55,480
The economy in the netherworld is as bad as it is in the mortal world.

211
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,480
So he'll take any chance to be greedy.

212
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:02,360
Plus, the King of Hell is fickle.

213
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:05,040
So the sooner we resolve this, the better.

214
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:09,760
As long as you stay focused and help me,

215
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:11,280
it should be fine.

216
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:14,800
What about after I help you?

217
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,800
Do I have to go back immediately after I'm done?

218
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:21,080
Go to my office tomorrow and find that draft first.

219
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:25,520
We'll worry about the rest later.

220
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,440
Don't you dare pull any tricks.

221
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:31,920
I'll be watching you from down there.

222
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:35,600
For anything urgent, take the mirror to my grave to find me.

223
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:05,440
Don't worry.

224
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,720
I won't leave you behind.

225
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:10,400
I'll find a way to stay alive.

226
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:30,959
(Negotiate with Shek Chung for more time in the mortal world.)

227
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:33,359
(Find out who killed me.)

228
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:35,760
(Doing evil deeds shortens lifespan. Does doing good deeds lengthen it?)

229
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:39,680
I hope it works.

230
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:28,720
What are you doing?

231
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,240
It's not ready yet.

232
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:38,840
I want to see the dashcam footage.

233
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,520
Who is this person?

234
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Say something.

235
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:50,160
What happened?

236
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:52,640
What did he do to you?

237
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:54,600
Send this video to me.

238
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:02,960
Hello?

239
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:05,360
I need all the CCTV footage near Lok Wing Road...

240
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:06,840
at 1am last night.

241
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,000
I'm looking for someone.

242
00:20:09,001 --> 00:20:10,080
I'll send you the video in a bit.

243
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:13,279
My car enthusiast friends are great at finding people.

244
00:20:13,280 --> 00:20:14,280
They can help.

245
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:21,720
Hurry up.

246
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:23,440
I just want to help you.

247
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:36,080
Amber.

248
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:42,160
I know you don't want me to know what's going on,

249
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:43,960
but I'm very worried about you.

250
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:47,520
This is a ballpoint pen on one end...

251
00:20:47,840 --> 00:20:48,840
and a spike on the other.

252
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,040
It can pierce through anything.

253
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:52,600
Take it for self-defense.

254
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:00,120
I'm only lending it to you.

255
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:02,720
You have to return it.

256
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:15,480
Ben.

257
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:19,640
Are you free?

258
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:21,680
I'm a bit busy today.

259
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:25,120
I'm feeling a bit down today.

260
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:27,360
Keep me company for a while.

261
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:37,760
Wait for me in the car.

262
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:43,800
I'll be right back.

263
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:47,880
She's Dee's wife.

264
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:50,120
So what? She's unhappy.

265
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:54,360
It's fine.

266
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:01,720
Excuse me.

267
00:22:02,080 --> 00:22:03,240
I'd like to make a donation.

268
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:04,760
What?

269
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:06,480
I'd like to make an offering.

270
00:22:08,320 --> 00:22:09,760
Just put it in that box.

271
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:16,520
Give me a certificate of appreciation...

272
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:19,520
to prove I'm charitable and earning merit.

273
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,000
I'll slowly add it in.

274
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:46,480
Red Cross Headquarters.

275
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,000
What's the matter?

276
00:22:57,360 --> 00:22:59,080
Didn't I tell you to go to my office?

277
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:00,920
Why are you dawdling here?

278
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:03,720
I forgot to call my boss.

279
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:08,800
Hello?

280
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:10,959
He said I've done too many bad things,

281
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:12,000
shortening my life.

282
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:14,320
So I'll do more good deeds now...

283
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:16,720
to make sure I don't die right after helping you.

284
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:19,520
If I'm going to die right after completing your case,

285
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:20,600
then I'll definitely delay it.

286
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:21,600
You can't delay it!

287
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:25,440
The trial is ongoing. We need a quick resolution.

288
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:27,520
Go to my office now.

289
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:30,000
Fine, but let's go to the Red Cross first.

290
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:31,600
Because if I don't go today...

291
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:33,920
If you don't focus on this case,

292
00:23:34,560 --> 00:23:36,839
I'll have the King of Hell take you back...

293
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:37,960
to have your tongue cut out!

294
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:42,880
Fine, I'll go. You don't have to be so fierce.

295
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:57,080
Counselor Yau is my apprentice.

296
00:23:57,720 --> 00:23:58,720
She's trustworthy.

297
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:02,120
How did you know my dad's will is in the office?

298
00:24:05,280 --> 00:24:06,280
I'm not at liberty to say.

299
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:08,200
How we find it doesn't matter.

300
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:09,640
What matters is the result.

301
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:13,320
In terms of investigation, if Counselor Yau is second,

302
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:14,600
even I wouldn't dare claim to be first.

303
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:15,960
She's absolutely trustworthy.

304
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:40,680
This way.

305
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,720
This unfilial son hasn't been back to the office for so long.

306
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:51,640
He doesn't even know where my room is.

307
00:24:53,360 --> 00:24:54,440
Could it be over there?

308
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:56,240
That looks like the boss's office.

309
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:23,440
Where is it?

310
00:25:23,680 --> 00:25:27,320
It's...

311
00:25:28,720 --> 00:25:29,720
Over there.

312
00:25:42,560 --> 00:25:44,480
Move those CDs, and you'll see a wooden box.

313
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:45,560
I put it inside.

314
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:50,880
Why do you...

315
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:53,040
Results are everything.

316
00:26:16,760 --> 00:26:18,000
I forgot where I put the key.

317
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:19,520
Let me think about it.

318
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:24,040
Is it okay as long as I can open it?

319
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:25,880
Yes.

320
00:26:43,840 --> 00:26:44,840
Thank you.

321
00:27:01,360 --> 00:27:02,760
Impossible.

322
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:14,840
- Hey. - You...

323
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:17,960
Stomachache.

324
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:19,760
Where's the restroom?

325
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:22,000
Over there.

326
00:27:31,880 --> 00:27:32,880
Her stomach hurts.

327
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:39,800
Are you kidding me?

328
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:42,240
I'm sure I put it in there.

329
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:43,960
It's one thing to drag me down,

330
00:27:44,280 --> 00:27:45,520
but now you're dragging my master down too.

331
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:47,400
How is he supposed to explain this to the client?

332
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:51,160
A real man takes responsibility for his own actions.

333
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:52,640
I'll apologize to your master.

334
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:54,600
Can he even see you?

335
00:27:59,640 --> 00:28:00,640
Think carefully.

336
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:02,880
Did you tell anyone else?

337
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:05,040
Could someone else have taken it?

338
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:09,080
I remember now.

339
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:11,600
That day, after I finished writing it at home...

340
00:28:28,080 --> 00:28:29,080
Chung!

341
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:33,000
Take your medicine first.

342
00:28:44,960 --> 00:28:45,960
Take it slow.

343
00:28:46,520 --> 00:28:47,520
Where is the master?

344
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:48,640
He's in the study.

345
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:50,080
Why weren't you following him?

346
00:28:50,800 --> 00:28:52,480
Always daydreaming.

347
00:28:52,560 --> 00:28:55,200
Put it away first. Keep it in the wooden box at the office.

348
00:28:58,120 --> 00:28:59,120
Here's the key.

349
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:06,480
That's how it was, right? You're not misremembering?

350
00:29:07,640 --> 00:29:09,160
That's right. I remember correctly.

351
00:29:10,160 --> 00:29:11,160
I really don't understand.

352
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:13,600
Why didn't you just have a lawyer handle it?

353
00:29:13,680 --> 00:29:14,920
It would've been safe at a law firm.

354
00:29:15,560 --> 00:29:17,120
We were married for so many years.

355
00:29:17,200 --> 00:29:19,280
I wanted to leave some room for reconciliation.

356
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:21,000
Who knew that evil woman...

357
00:29:21,080 --> 00:29:22,239
wouldn't even visit me once...

358
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:23,680
while I was in the hospital for so long?

359
00:29:24,520 --> 00:29:26,400
We shared a bed for decades.

360
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:29,920
I didn't see her true colors until the moment I died.

361
00:29:33,440 --> 00:29:34,480
I can't stay.

362
00:29:34,840 --> 00:29:36,519
I've been in the world of the living too long.

363
00:29:36,520 --> 00:29:37,680
I have to go back.

364
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:41,360
Go to Kwan Nga and get the will.

365
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:46,560
She was my former nurse. Hurry.

366
00:29:58,920 --> 00:29:59,920
Where is Mr. Shek?

367
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:01,200
He's gone.

368
00:30:03,400 --> 00:30:04,880
I'll definitely find that draft...

369
00:30:05,760 --> 00:30:07,120
so you can fulfill your promise to Mr. Shek.

370
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:09,000
You're doing me a favor by helping.

371
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:10,800
Don't make it sound like it's your responsibility.

372
00:30:11,120 --> 00:30:12,120
Get in the car.

373
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:23,440
Are you free tonight?

374
00:30:23,800 --> 00:30:25,240
Dinner to celebrate your birthday?

375
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:28,200
Has your wife recovered?

376
00:30:29,120 --> 00:30:30,160
Almost.

377
00:30:31,640 --> 00:30:32,760
(Wife)

378
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:36,960
Hello?

379
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:44,720
Okay, I'll be right back. Bye.

380
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:48,919
I'm sorry.

381
00:30:48,920 --> 00:30:49,920
It's okay.

382
00:32:08,440 --> 00:32:09,520
Please help me one more time.

383
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:12,840
I'm begging you.

384
00:32:26,480 --> 00:32:27,920
It's hard to get stock lately. Take them sparingly.

385
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:52,520
Can I have one more? Thank you.

386
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:16,760
When did you start taking these again?

387
00:33:21,560 --> 00:33:22,560
The odds for this case...

388
00:33:23,880 --> 00:33:25,040
have always been low.

389
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:29,560
But I represent the side of justice.

390
00:33:32,200 --> 00:33:34,600
My wife, my father-in-law,

391
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:37,600
and the whole world thinks I'll win.

392
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:41,240
I'll definitely find that draft.

393
00:33:45,080 --> 00:33:46,320
How do you know it exists?

394
00:33:48,680 --> 00:33:49,800
I know his nurse.

395
00:34:00,320 --> 00:34:01,360
I'm really losing my touch.

396
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:04,360
I even missed a key point like this.

397
00:34:11,280 --> 00:34:12,280
That's enough.

398
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:19,240
I don't want to do...

399
00:34:20,720 --> 00:34:21,760
shady things anymore.

400
00:34:25,120 --> 00:34:26,160
Let's change our ways together, okay?

401
00:34:34,600 --> 00:34:35,600
I'll take you home first.

402
00:34:37,600 --> 00:34:39,040
The medicine made me thirsty.

403
00:34:40,080 --> 00:34:41,400
Can you buy me a bottle of water?

404
00:35:14,240 --> 00:35:15,880
Master.

405
00:35:16,840 --> 00:35:17,840
Master!

406
00:35:28,120 --> 00:35:29,120
Send an ambulance immediately.

407
00:35:29,121 --> 00:35:30,480
I'm on First Street. Someone fainted.

408
00:35:32,640 --> 00:35:33,640
What should I do now?

409
00:35:34,960 --> 00:35:35,960
CPR?

410
00:35:36,680 --> 00:35:37,720
I don't know how to do CPR.

411
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:39,360
I'll go find someone.

412
00:35:45,280 --> 00:35:47,400
Do you know how to perform CPR?

413
00:35:50,520 --> 00:35:51,840
Sir, do you know how to perform CPR?

414
00:35:52,080 --> 00:35:53,680
CPR.

415
00:36:07,680 --> 00:36:09,200
Master.

416
00:36:09,680 --> 00:36:11,560
The ambulance is here. Hang in there.

417
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:13,880
Please be okay.

418
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:17,120
You have to be okay.

419
00:36:40,920 --> 00:36:41,920
I didn't say anything.

420
00:36:42,880 --> 00:36:44,720
I've arranged to transfer you to Yan Wo.

421
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:47,400
Dr. Chan will follow up.

422
00:36:48,560 --> 00:36:50,920
No need. I'm fine. Help me process my discharge.

423
00:36:53,760 --> 00:36:54,880
Did my wife look for me?

424
00:36:56,200 --> 00:36:57,200
I've asked Bella to tell her...

425
00:36:57,280 --> 00:36:58,280
that you need to review a case tonight.

426
00:36:59,800 --> 00:37:00,800
Thank you.

427
00:37:03,960 --> 00:37:04,960
I'm sorry.

428
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:09,400
Think about what you really want.

429
00:37:10,920 --> 00:37:12,160
Is this how you want to keep going?

430
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:18,400
I'm leaving. Get some rest.

431
00:37:19,360 --> 00:37:20,360
Where are the pills?

432
00:37:23,160 --> 00:37:24,200
They're still in your car.

433
00:37:24,920 --> 00:37:25,920
Don't worry.

434
00:37:27,080 --> 00:37:29,319
Tomorrow, I'll be...

435
00:37:29,320 --> 00:37:30,840
the same Yeung Kam Tsuen that you all know.

436
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:32,760
Don't worry.

437
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:01,360
Please focus.

438
00:38:02,760 --> 00:38:04,720
What clues have we missed?

439
00:38:05,600 --> 00:38:07,880
Didn't I say there was a draft?

440
00:38:07,960 --> 00:38:09,240
Go find Kwan Nga.

441
00:38:10,560 --> 00:38:12,040
What are you still digging for here?

442
00:38:12,360 --> 00:38:14,120
I've already sent someone to find her.

443
00:38:14,200 --> 00:38:15,760
One can never have too much evidence, old man.

444
00:38:16,200 --> 00:38:17,200
You're calling me an old man?

445
00:38:17,800 --> 00:38:20,720
I'm strong enough to kill tigers! Old man?

446
00:38:25,160 --> 00:38:26,160
Wait.

447
00:38:27,520 --> 00:38:28,800
That ungrateful son...

448
00:38:29,280 --> 00:38:31,600
installed CCTV at the front door.

449
00:38:32,920 --> 00:38:34,040
What were they saying that day?

450
00:38:35,640 --> 00:38:36,640
Does it record audio?

451
00:38:37,080 --> 00:38:38,320
The one at my house does.

452
00:38:39,240 --> 00:38:41,480
That ungrateful son must have used the same technician.

453
00:38:53,040 --> 00:38:55,320
While Mr. Shek Chung was being treated for lung cancer,

454
00:38:55,920 --> 00:38:59,240
you transferred about 30 million in cash from his accounts...

455
00:38:59,560 --> 00:39:01,720
into your personal account, right?

456
00:39:02,400 --> 00:39:03,960
- Yes. - Why did you do that?

457
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:06,920
Those were birthday gifts from him.

458
00:39:07,320 --> 00:39:09,720
He was in poor health and authorized me to handle it.

459
00:39:10,200 --> 00:39:12,800
Why would he suddenly transfer 30 million in cash...

460
00:39:12,880 --> 00:39:14,200
to you as a birthday gift?

461
00:39:14,960 --> 00:39:17,080
Maybe he knew his time was short.

462
00:39:17,600 --> 00:39:18,760
He wanted to provide me with security.

463
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:22,200
That's strange.

464
00:39:23,360 --> 00:39:25,440
You are Shek Chung's legal wife.

465
00:39:26,080 --> 00:39:27,440
Even if he didn't have a will,

466
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:31,480
half of his estate would go to you after his death.

467
00:39:31,960 --> 00:39:33,720
Was it because your relationship changed?

468
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:36,720
He didn't like you, and you were afraid he would divorce you,

469
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:38,040
so you transferred the money?

470
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:39,840
Your Honor, I object.

471
00:39:39,920 --> 00:39:42,000
No. I'm Mrs. Shek, and I always will be.

472
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:43,800
Don't talk nonsense here.

473
00:39:44,640 --> 00:39:46,800
Witness, please watch your language.

474
00:39:49,880 --> 00:39:53,040
Please turn to page 33 of the bundle.

475
00:39:59,160 --> 00:40:00,160
Who is she?

476
00:40:02,360 --> 00:40:03,360
She was my husband's nurse.

477
00:40:04,840 --> 00:40:08,040
She was Mr. Shek Chung's nurse, Ms. Leung Kwan Nga.

478
00:40:08,920 --> 00:40:12,360
You complained about her to the agency many times.

479
00:40:12,880 --> 00:40:13,880
Yes.

480
00:40:14,080 --> 00:40:16,080
Because she did a poor job and was irresponsible.

481
00:40:17,600 --> 00:40:19,720
If she was so bad, why didn't you fire her?

482
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:24,240
Because Chung always said to give young people a chance.

483
00:40:24,560 --> 00:40:27,160
Now, playing the footage referenced on page 40,

484
00:40:27,240 --> 00:40:28,840
a clip on the USB drive.

485
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:32,640
It is CCTV footage showing the defendant, Shek Kwong Sing,

486
00:40:32,720 --> 00:40:36,320
outside his own home.

487
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:04,360
Can you explain what was happening then?

488
00:41:06,120 --> 00:41:08,959
The nurse took Chung away without my permission.

489
00:41:08,960 --> 00:41:09,960
I was arguing with her.

490
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:12,560
Why do you keep asking about that woman?

491
00:41:12,640 --> 00:41:14,160
She has nothing to do with our family matters.

492
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:15,800
Your Honor,

493
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:19,280
Ms. Leung is highly relevant to this case.

494
00:41:19,720 --> 00:41:21,880
Please allow me to play the video again.

495
00:41:23,960 --> 00:41:25,920
Please turn the volume to the maximum.

496
00:41:27,040 --> 00:41:28,360
It actually has audio.

497
00:41:28,680 --> 00:41:30,240
The recording is just very faint.

498
00:41:30,720 --> 00:41:32,760
It's so quiet that no one noticed,

499
00:41:33,080 --> 00:41:34,680
but we have prepared an amplifier.
